{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/479457-new-exploit-manifold-angles","id":479457,"title":"New Exploit: Manifold Angles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-13T14:11:43-07:00","id":479457,"title":"New Exploit: Manifold Angles","content":"In the Genesis 3:24, after Adam and Eve are expelled from Eden, God sends an angel to protect the Garden. This angel has a flaming sword which &quot;strikes in all directions at once&quot;. A Demon with this Exploit can't warp space in such vast ways, but he can impose great obstacles and give punishments to invaders.<br /> <br /> Example Prerequisites: Diversion (Mundane), Ambush (Instrumental), Left Or Right? (Cacophony)<br /> <br /> Dice Roll: Intelligence + Subterfuge + Primum<br /> <br /> Action: Extended (target number = 15, with each roll taking one turn)<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Aether per roll<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: a bonus for invaders to infiltrate equal to the Demon's Primum, capping at +5.<br /> <br /> Failure: no progress is made.<br /> <br /> Success: a &quot;flaming sword&quot; is established over a radius of 50 yards per dot of Primum. The Demon may make the area smaller than that, if he wishes. All invaders find that space itself warps to banish them, making certain doors, windows, corridors and the like lead to new locations. Evading these spatial distortions requires Wits + Investigation, with NO willpower boost and a penalty equal to the Demon's Intelligence. The Demon has to specify 4 criteria that can bypass this protection. This Exploit lasts for one scene. An additional Aether may be spent to add ONE of the following setbacks:<br /> <br /> A) The Exploit lasts for 24 hours.<br /> <br /> B) Any invader which fails his roll suffers a number of bashing damage equal to the Demon's Intelligence + Primum caused by spatial distortions inside his body. This damage ignores Armor but does NOT upgrade into lethal<br /> <br /> C) Any invader which fails his roll loses one important item. This can include objects such a camera, gun, wallet or merely something of emotional importance.<br /> <br /> D) Any invader which fails his roll loses half of their current Aether or Essence, as finely tuned spatial distortions siphon their energies into some place between places. These points flow back to them after the Exploit fades.<br /> <br /> E) The Demon which used the Exploit can create spatial &quot;chains&quot; between himself and invaders which fail the roll. The Demon knows they have invaded, can feel their direction and distance and gains +4 to spot and follow them, through foot or vehicle. These &quot;chains&quot; end when the Exploit fades.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: two of the above setbacks may be added.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-13-2015, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T15:51:26-07:00","id":479577,"title":"","content":"I like it, the only reason I feel it isn't unbalanced as an exploit is the attention this ironically could draw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T16:37:25-07:00","id":479607,"title":"","content":"Excessively fiddly. Pick a Skill to base it off of, set the area to a radius based on a multiple of one Trait instead of three-with-a-variable, pick one range-expander criterion, drop or require the number of bypass vectors, and for the love of Beelzebub make it an extended action to vent the expanders and give you an outlet for exceptional success customization.<br /> <br /> Also maybe key it off of Intelligence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T17:18:00-07:00","id":479621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/479457-new-exploit-manifold-angles?p=479607#post479607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excessively fiddly. Pick a Skill to base it off of, set the area to a radius based on a multiple of one Trait instead 